<title>SPAIN: Intervention rumours keep Spain peseta at 84.75/DM.</title>
<headline>Intervention rumours keep Spain peseta at 84.75/DM.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The peseta, plagued by a weaker Italian lira, fell to 84.75 per mark where it was stopped by rumours of central bank intervention, dealers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Bank of Spain did not, as is its practice, comment on these rumours.</p>
<p>At around 1440 GMT the peseta was trading at around 84.72/4.75 per mark versus an opening level of 84.54/59.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
